<title>MEXICO: Mexico says single consortium left in rail bidding.</title>
<headline>Mexico says single consortium left in rail bidding.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bidding in the privatization of Mexico's largest railway has been narrowed to one consortium from three initial bidders, a Mexican Communications and Transport Ministry (SCT) official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Mexican builder Empresas ICA and U.S. Union Pacific Corp decided to join forces with Mexican miner Grupo Mexico on the bid for the Pacific-North railroad, the ministry's privatization coordinator, Jorge Silberstein, told Reuters.</p>
